 OH + HO2 = O2 + H2O                              :  4.80E-11     0.000     -250.0 :    300     2000 : A : 1994BAU, agrees with recent experimental data at 298 K and up to 2200 K
 OH + H2O2 = HO2 + H2O                            :  3.60E-13     1.625     -530.0 :     96     1460 : A : fit to 2003VAK (96-296 K), 2004JIM (254-356 K), and 2010HON (1020-1460 K)
 OH + O3 = O2 + HO2                               :  6.70E-13     1.690      694.0 :    100     2000 : A : fit to 2020BUR (190-357 K) and 2007JU (100 K and 500-2000 K)
!OH + CH3CO = OH + CO + CH3                       :  5.00E-11     0.000        0.0 :    300     2500 : B : 1986TSA, endothermic by 46.5 kJ/mol, this is a thermal dissociation involving OH as collider
 O2 + H2 = O + H2O                                :  4.20E-11     0.510    35540.0 :    298     1000 : B : 1999KAR
!O2 + CH3CO = CH2CO + O + OH                      :  3.20E-12     0.000        0.0 :    220      500 : B : 2005BAU, CH2COO assumed to decompose as CH2CO + O but reaction is endothermic by 247.2 kJ/mol
