!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!
!
!
! Large hydrocarbons are neglected
!
!
! CH2O2: this is a Criegee intermediate that appear in evaluations of atmospheric chemistry
!
!
! CH2OOH: isomer of CH3O2 that has a poorly documented chemistry
!
!
! C2H3OH: isomer of CH3CHO, only a few reactions documented 
!
!
! O-bearing molecules with more than one C atom are neglected
!
! CH3CO
! (CHO)2
! CH3CO2
! C2H3O2
! CH3OCO
! CH3COOH
! CH3CHO2
! HCOCH2OH
! C2H5O2
! C2H4OOH
! C2H5OOH
! CH3CO3
! CH3CO3H
! HC3O
! C3H2O
! C3H3O
! CH2CHCHO
! C2H3CHO
! CH3COCH2
! CH3COCH3
! C3H6O
! C3H6OH
! n-C3H7O
! i-C3H7O
! C3H7O2
!
!
! N_2D: excited N neglected
!
!
! N-bearing molecules with more than two N atoms are neglected
!
! N3
! HN3
! HNNNH2
!
!
! N-bearing molecules with two N atoms and carbon are neglected
!
! NCN
! CN2
! CHN2
! CH2N2
! NH2CN
! CH2NNH2
! CH3NNH
! ONCN
!
!
! N-bearing molecules with poorly documented chemistry
!
! HCCN
! CH3CHNH
! C2H5NH
! CH3NHCN
! C3N
! CH3C3N
! CH2CCHCN
! HCCCH2CN
! C4H5N
! C5H2N
! NC4N
! N2O4
! N2O5
! HOONO
! NH2NO2
! NH2ONO
! HONHO
! HCOHN
! HO2NO2
! CH3ONO
! CH3ONO2
! CH3O2NO2
! HCOCN
! CH3CONO
! C2H5NO2
! C2H5ONO
! C2H5ONO2
! C2H5O2NO2
! HCOCHCN
! n-C3H7ONO
! i-C3H7ONO
! n-C3H7ONO2
! i-C3H7ONO2
!
!
! HON: isomer of HNO, formed by NCO + OH according to 2000DEA, but not according to 2001CAM. We neglect it because of the uncertain formation in NCO + OH. Thermochemical data in 2000DEA need to be fitted to polynomials.
!
!
! HNNO, NH2NO, H2NNHO, HNO2, HNOO: species that appear widely in 2000DEA, but no thermochemical data in databases. Check to get it from 2000DEA.
!    HNO2 is an isomer of HONO. HNOO is a third less stable isomer introduced by 2000DEA (see 2000DEA p 260). HNOO is only formed by NH + O2 and then dissociates to NO + OH. None of them have thermochemical data in databases.
!
!
! H2SiO, TiS
!
!
!
